From: Rob Vogelaar <rob.vogelaar@libertyglobal.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 16:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] agent: suppress withdrawn stations in topology response

Station-list notification and aggregation stages are asynchronous.  A full
snapshot can therefore leave the same STA/BSSID/RUID key briefly present in
both the consolidated association map and the disassociation map.  The
Topology Notification correctly publishes the withdrawal, but a Topology
Response emitted during that convergence window previously serialized the
stale live row.  Its freshly reconstructed Association Time made the
controller select the former AP as the newer owner and reversed a completed
roam until a later withdrawal repaired it.

Treat a matching disassociation tombstone as newer than the consolidated row
when constructing the Associated Clients TLV.  A genuine reassociation
already removes that tombstone in the station aggregate path, so it remains
eligible for the next complete snapshot.  Add regression coverage for the
conflicting-map state observed in the live lab.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 inc/em_configuration.h           |  9 +++++++++
 src/em/config/em_configuration.cpp | 23 +++++++++++++++++++++--
 tests/test_l1_em_orch_agent.cpp  | 22 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 52 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/inc/em_configuration.h
+++ b/inc/em_configuration.h
@@ -1609,6 +1609,15 @@
 
 public:
 	/**
+	 * Return true only when a station row is safe to advertise as associated.
+	 * A disassociation tombstone for the same STA/BSSID/RUID is authoritative
+	 * while asynchronous station-list stages converge and must suppress a
+	 * stale live-map row.
+	 */
+	static bool is_advertisable_association(dm_easy_mesh_t *dm,
+		const em_sta_info_t& sta_info);
+
+	/**
 	 * Apply a non-MLO station withdrawal to the controller's live and pending
 	 * station maps. Topology Notifications carry a normal STA MAC but no
 	 * Associated STA MLD entry, so they must not depend on MLO metadata to
--- a/src/em/config/em_configuration.cpp
+++ b/src/em/config/em_configuration.cpp
@@ -1558,6 +1558,25 @@
     return static_cast<int> (len);
 }
 
+bool em_configuration_t::is_advertisable_association(
+        dm_easy_mesh_t *dm, const em_sta_info_t& sta_info)
+{
+    if (dm == NULL || !sta_info.associated) {
+        return false;
+    }
+
+    /* Association and disassociation commands are intentionally staged on
+     * independent objects.  During that short convergence window both maps
+     * can contain the same key.  The withdrawal is the newer ownership
+     * evidence; advertising the stale live row resets Association Time and
+     * can make the controller move the STA back to its previous AP. */
+    return dm->get_sta_info(
+            const_cast<unsigned char *>(sta_info.id),
+            const_cast<unsigned char *>(sta_info.bssid),
+            const_cast<unsigned char *>(sta_info.radiomac),
+            em_target_sta_map_disassoc) == NULL;
+}
+
 int em_configuration_t::create_associated_clients_tlv(unsigned char *buff,
                                                        unsigned int capacity)
 {
@@ -1590,7 +1609,7 @@
 
         sta = static_cast<dm_sta_t *>(hash_map_get_first(dm->m_sta_map));
         while (sta != NULL) {
-            if (sta->m_sta_info.associated &&
+            if (is_advertisable_association(dm, sta->m_sta_info) &&
                     memcmp(sta->m_sta_info.bssid, bss->bssid.mac,
                            sizeof(bssid_t)) == 0) {
                 sta_count++;
@@ -1617,7 +1636,7 @@
 
